# --- Replacing and splitting --------------------------------------------
## Functional form of `replace`: replace the first occurrence.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `from_str`: the text to replace.
## - `to_str`: the replacement text.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.replace with "abc", "b", "X"    # "aXc"
## ```
weave replace with s as string, from_str as string, to_str as string into string:
    return calling s.replace with from_str, to_str
## Functional form of `replace_all`: replace every non-overlapping occurrence.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `from_str`: the text to replace; empty changes nothing.
## - `to_str`: the replacement text.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.replace_all with "aaa", "a", "b"    # "bbb"
## ```
weave replace_all with s as string, from_str as string, to_str as string into string:
    return calling s.replace_all with from_str, to_str
## Functional form of `split`: split on every delimiter.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `delim`: the separator; empty keeps the whole string.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of string`; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.split with "a,b", ","    # ["a", "b"]
## ```
weave split with s as string, delim as string into list of string:
    return calling s.split with delim
## Functional form of `splitn`: split into at most `n` parts.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `delim`: the separator; empty keeps the whole string.
## - `n`: maximum number of parts; `n <= 0` performs no split.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of string`; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.splitn with "a,b,c", ",", 2    # ["a", "b,c"]
## ```
weave splitn with s as string, delim as string, n as int into list of string:
    return calling s.splitn with delim, n
## Functional form of `rsplit`: split scanning from the right.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `delim`: the separator; empty keeps the whole string.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of string` in left-to-right order; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.rsplit with "a:b:c", ":"    # ["a", "b", "c"]
## ```
weave rsplit with s as string, delim as string into list of string:
    return calling s.rsplit with delim
## Functional form of `repeat`: repeat `s` `count` times.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to repeat.
## - `count`: the number of copies.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; `count <= 0` or empty `s` yields "". Release it with
## `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
